 150:memory.h      **** /*
 151:memory.h      **** When the system starts up, the BIOS/boot program collects the memory mapping information. 
 152:memory.h      **** The boot program stores the mapping table at the designated location (such as physical address 0x7e
 153:memory.h      **** During the kernel initialization, a page table mapping is established to make this physical address
 154:memory.h      **** The kernel code reads and parses these entries through pointers. 
 155:memory.h      **** The kernel builds the physical memory management data structure based on this information.
 156:memory.h      **** 
 157:memory.h      **** E820 is a convenient tool for BIOS of X86-based computer systems to map memory to the operating sys
 158:memory.h      **** By setting the AX register to the hexadecimal value E820, it can be accessed through the INT15H cal
 159:memory.h      **** reporting which memory address ranges are available and which are reserved for use by the BIOS.
 160:memory.h      **** */
